# Approval Gates

## Automatic Approval Triggers
After every task planning:
1. Run complexity scoring (1-10 scale)
2. If score ≥ 7 → needs_review = true
3. If priority = Critical → needs_review = true
4. If cross-system impact → needs_review = true

## Complexity Scoring Guide
- 1-3: Single file, localized, well-understood patterns
- 4-6: Multiple files, moderate complexity, established patterns
- 7-8: Cross-system changes, new patterns, coordination required
- 9-10: Architectural impact, multiple systems, high risk

## Mandatory Approval Required For
- Architectural changes (system redesigns, new managers, core pattern modifications)
- File structure changes (splitting files, creating new managers, directory restructuring)
- Core system modifications (Enumerations.cs, Unity lifecycle, manager communication patterns)
- Documentation changes (creating new documentation files)

## Pre-Approved Patterns (No Approval Needed)
- Adding debug logging to existing methods
- Creating POC implementations (marked appropriately)
- Optimizing existing code without changing interfaces
- Adding validation checks
- Improving error handling
